Oh.

256
00:12:41,343 --> 00:12:42,845
Someone's ringing my phone.

257
00:12:44,346 --> 00:12:45,598
Chief,

258
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:46,974
she's on her way up.

259
00:12:47,057 --> 00:12:48,184
Okay.

260
00:12:48,267 --> 00:12:50,936
Just stand by in case she needs something.

261
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:52,938
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

262
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,733
Ms. Lindsay!

263
00:12:56,775 --> 00:12:58,068
Hi, Ms. Lindsay!

264
00:12:58,152 --> 00:13:00,279
We had food brought in for you. Dig in.

265
00:13:00,362 --> 00:13:01,697
- Dig in.
- If you have any food request,

266
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:02,823
just let us know.

267
00:13:02,907 --> 00:13:04,074
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

268
00:13:04,158 --> 00:13:05,326
Feel free.

269
00:13:05,409 --> 00:13:06,827
[BILLY CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

270
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:10,789
Billy, where did you get
the concept of LoveFeast?

271
00:13:10,873 --> 00:13:15,294
It was actually inspired
by a wedding proposal.

272
00:13:17,379 --> 00:13:18,464
From here?

273
00:13:18,547 --> 00:13:21,175
[FEMALE VO] <i>You found love at Pebblng.</i>

274
00:13:21,258 --> 00:13:23,969
<i>And now, we're celebrating it!</i>

275
00:13:24,053 --> 00:13:27,431
<i>In our new feature,</i>
<i>we will sponsor the wedding</i>

276
00:13:27,515 --> 00:13:30,142
<i>of couples who matched on Pebblng,</i>

277
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:33,270
<i>turning swipes into "I do's"!</i>

278
00:13:33,354 --> 00:13:37,733
<i>Because all love stories</i>
<i>deserve a happy ending.</i>

279
00:13:39,693 --> 00:13:41,654
You can forget about the contract.

280
00:13:41,737 --> 00:13:42,988
I'm not signing.

281
00:13:44,365 --> 00:13:46,700
You know, I was prepared
to invest on LoveFeast.

282
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:49,078
I really love the concept.

283
00:13:49,161 --> 00:13:52,790
But, apparently, it's a replica
of an existing concept.

284
00:13:52,873 --> 00:13:55,334
That's a serious matter, Billy!

285
00:13:55,417 --> 00:13:59,630
My name is built on integrity,
and I plan to protect that.

286
00:13:59,713 --> 00:14:01,340
Yeah, I understand, Ms. Lindsay,

287
00:14:01,423 --> 00:14:05,594
but I can assure you
that LoveFeast is our original idea.

288
00:14:07,096 --> 00:14:09,014
Let me look into it immediately.

289
00:14:09,807 --> 00:14:11,600
Don't waste your time.

290
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:13,102
You already wasted mine.

291
00:14:24,238 --> 00:14:25,948
[LINE RINGS]

292
00:14:26,699 --> 00:14:29,869
Bea. Bea, why aren't you answering?!

293
00:14:30,828 --> 00:14:32,329
[LINE RINGS]

294
00:14:33,455 --> 00:14:35,499
- Bea? Bea!
- [LINE RINGS]

295
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:38,210
- [LINE DISCONNECTS]
- Argh!

296
00:14:41,755 --> 00:14:43,757
She might leave me too.

297
00:14:43,841 --> 00:14:46,510
Abi, you already left me.

298
00:14:48,387 --> 00:14:50,931
Your father left me as well.

299
00:14:52,558 --> 00:14:53,559
[CRIES]

300
00:14:54,435 --> 00:14:55,436
[SNIFFLES]

301
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:57,646
Bea…

302
00:14:58,439 --> 00:15:01,567
You cannot leave me.

303
00:15:04,778 --> 00:15:05,821
You can't.

304
00:15:07,281 --> 00:15:08,282
[PICTURE FRAME THUDS]

305
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:11,285
[BAG THUDS]

306
00:15:13,078 --> 00:15:14,955
I will find you.

307
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:17,499
I will figure out what you're hiding.

308
00:15:18,834 --> 00:15:20,419
- [SCREAMING]
- [BAG THUDS]

309
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:23,047
[GRUNTS]

310
00:15:25,090 --> 00:15:30,930
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

311
00:15:35,434 --> 00:15:37,186
An exact copy.

312
00:15:37,937 --> 00:15:39,980
Could this also have been
Shirley De Leon's work?

313
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:42,858
I mean, she was once Caloy's boss.

314
00:15:44,234 --> 00:15:46,570
This is clearly an inside job.

315
00:15:47,404 --> 00:15:49,865
We're the only ones
who know about LoveFeast.

316
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:52,993
How would Shirley know
if she isn't even here?

317
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:55,371
True.

318
00:15:55,454 --> 00:15:58,415
Then, the one that leaked LoveFeast

319
00:15:58,499 --> 00:16:00,542
must be among us.

320
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,836
[VALERIE SCOFFS]

321
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:05,339
Wow, I can't believe this.

322
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:07,883
After everything I did for this company,

323
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:10,094
you dare accuse me?

324
00:16:10,177 --> 00:16:12,429
- Who else?
- Enough!

325
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:15,891
This will not solve anything.

326
00:16:15,975 --> 00:16:19,353
Tell me. What would I gain
if I leaked LoveFeast to the competition?

327
00:16:20,145 --> 00:16:22,648
What? You guys still think this
is about Jordan, huh?

328
00:16:22,731 --> 00:16:25,109
FYI, I have a new boyfriend,

329
00:16:25,192 --> 00:16:27,236
and I'm so over Jordan!

330
00:16:27,319 --> 00:16:28,696
We're just friends, okay?

331
00:16:28,779 --> 00:16:30,114
[BLAIRE] Exactly!

332
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:31,448
Plus one there, girl!

333
00:16:31,532 --> 00:16:34,243
My twin has found herself a new boyfriend!

334
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:36,245
You should watch her vlogs.

335
00:16:36,328 --> 00:16:38,455
They've already gone full hard launch.

336
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:40,833
So, who leaked it?

337
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:43,419
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

338
00:16:43,502 --> 00:16:45,337
There's only one way to find out.

339
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:48,424
Excuse me.

340
00:16:49,383 --> 00:16:50,843
[BIRDS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE]

341
00:16:50,926 --> 00:16:54,013
We really don't know any Bea, ma'am.

342
00:16:54,596 --> 00:16:57,391
Look, she's my daughter.

343
00:16:57,474 --> 00:16:59,351
I saw this among her things.

344
00:17:00,352 --> 00:17:02,104
She works here.

345
00:17:03,063 --> 00:17:06,984
Uh, there's no Bea working here.

346
00:17:07,067 --> 00:17:09,361
You might want to call her first.

347
00:17:09,987 --> 00:17:12,072
She's not even picking up my calls.

348
00:17:13,449 --> 00:17:14,742
I'm sorry.

349
00:17:14,825 --> 00:17:16,952
No Bea is employed here.

350
00:17:17,953 --> 00:17:22,541
Don't tell me she said
she doesn't want to talk to me.

351
00:17:23,292 --> 00:17:24,334
Sorry?

352
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:26,045
Just admit it!

353
00:17:26,128 --> 00:17:27,254
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

354
00:17:27,337 --> 00:17:29,673
She's hiding from me, isn't she?

355
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:32,676
She's not planning on coming back?
She's never coming home?

356
00:17:33,302 --> 00:17:34,595
[BREATHES SHARPLY]

357
00:17:34,678 --> 00:17:36,388
- Bea!
- [PRECIOUS] Uh…

358
00:17:37,848 --> 00:17:38,974
Bea?

359
00:17:40,225 --> 00:17:42,436
Bea, sweetheart, come out!

360
00:17:43,645 --> 00:17:44,980
Bea!

361
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:46,857
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

362
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:48,609
Bea!

363
00:17:48,692 --> 00:17:51,320
- Ma'am…
- Where's my daughter?

364
00:17:51,403 --> 00:17:52,905
- Show her…
- Calm down.

365
00:17:52,988 --> 00:17:54,615
- Bea!
- Take it easy.

366
00:17:54,698 --> 00:17:55,616
- Guard!
- Let me.

367
00:17:55,699 --> 00:17:57,326
- [SCREAMING]
- Oh my…

368
00:17:57,409 --> 00:18:00,287
- I'll take it from here.
- Argh! Don't touch me!

369
00:18:00,370 --> 00:18:01,497
Please take a seat.

370
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:03,290
- Go ahead, sit down.
- Bea!

371
00:18:03,373 --> 00:18:04,625
Sweetheart!

372
00:18:04,708 --> 00:18:07,127
So, you're saying somebody
leaked the concept?

373
00:18:07,211 --> 00:18:09,671
I don't even know what happened.

374
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:11,090
Who do you think it is?

375
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:14,885
The girls think
it's either Shirley or Val,

376
00:18:14,968 --> 00:18:17,513
but my gut tells me that
it's neither of them.

377
00:18:17,596 --> 00:18:19,389
We can't just keep guessing.

378
00:18:19,473 --> 00:18:21,183
I'm on my way to Pebblng.

379
00:18:21,266 --> 00:18:23,102
Pebblng? Your batchmate's company?

380
00:18:23,185 --> 00:18:24,103
Yes.

381
00:18:24,186 --> 00:18:27,397
Their CEO is Camille Cordova.

382
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:30,901
She can't do to me again
what she did before.

383
00:18:31,652 --> 00:18:32,778
What did she do to you?

384
00:18:32,861 --> 00:18:35,364
Honestly, Ms. Camille,
I've been wanting to

385
00:18:35,447 --> 00:18:36,990
join your company for a long time.

386
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:38,826
Unfortunately, you weren't hiring.

387
00:18:38,909 --> 00:18:41,370
So today, I just went for it.

388
00:18:41,453 --> 00:18:44,289
And you're exactly what I want.

389
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:46,083
Someone who is brave,

390
00:18:46,166 --> 00:18:49,670
and someone who finally
thinks outside the box.

391
00:18:49,753 --> 00:18:50,838
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

392
00:18:50,921 --> 00:18:52,840
[BILLY] <i>We were academic rivals.</i>

393
00:18:52,923 --> 00:18:54,508
<i>I was summa, she was magna cum laude.</i>

394
00:18:54,591 --> 00:18:56,969
A day before the thesis topic proposal,

395
00:18:57,052 --> 00:18:59,138
I found out that we had the same idea.

396
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:03,392
It turned out, she had learned that
I had done initial research

397
00:19:03,475 --> 00:19:07,020
<i>about coping mechanisms</i>
<i>among women trauma survivors.</i>

398
00:19:07,646 --> 00:19:09,481
She stole my idea.

399
00:19:09,565 --> 00:19:12,568
Damn. So she wasn't just smart in school.

400
00:19:12,651 --> 00:19:14,194
She was also a thief.

401
00:19:15,028 --> 00:19:16,238
Why didn't I know this?

402
00:19:16,321 --> 00:19:17,739
Nah, dude. You were busy at the time,

403
00:19:17,823 --> 00:19:19,741
so I chose not to bother you.

404
00:19:19,825 --> 00:19:20,951
Well…

405
00:19:22,286 --> 00:19:25,622
Who could have leaked
LoveFeast to Camille?

406
00:19:25,706 --> 00:19:27,875
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

407
00:19:27,958 --> 00:19:29,459
[MUSIC FADES]

408
00:19:29,543 --> 00:19:32,462
[HEAVY FOOTSTEPS]

409
00:19:32,546 --> 00:19:34,506
[DOG BARKING IN DISTANCE]

410
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:40,470
Thank you for letting me rent
your apartment.

411
00:19:40,554 --> 00:19:41,889
You're welcome.

412
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:43,473
You're a hardworking man, Eric.

413
00:19:43,557 --> 00:19:46,101
The previous tenant just left.
It's perfect timing.

414
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:47,186
Wait here.

415
00:19:47,269 --> 00:19:48,645
I'll just open the gate.

416
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:50,564
- [HANDLE CLANKING]
- [GATE RATTLING]

417
00:19:50,647 --> 00:19:51,732
Come in.

418
00:19:51,815 --> 00:19:52,858
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

419
00:19:52,941 --> 00:19:54,067
[GRUNTS]

420
00:20:05,621 --> 00:20:08,540
Everyone I love…

421
00:20:09,333 --> 00:20:10,584
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

422
00:20:10,667 --> 00:20:14,213
They leave and never return.

423
00:20:15,547 --> 00:20:17,799
My daughter Bea?

424
00:20:19,009 --> 00:20:20,928
I know she wants to leave me.

425
00:20:22,137 --> 00:20:24,014
I understand you.

426
00:20:24,097 --> 00:20:26,600
I was abandoned by my father.

427
00:20:27,392 --> 00:20:29,102
And again

428
00:20:29,186 --> 00:20:30,479
by the man I loved.

429
00:20:30,562 --> 00:20:32,814
The man I was going to marry.

430
00:20:32,898 --> 00:20:34,775
So I know how you feel.

431
00:20:36,735 --> 00:20:38,570
I feel like

432
00:20:38,654 --> 00:20:41,615
Bea won't come back to me.

433
00:20:41,698 --> 00:20:44,326
She'll leave me.

434
00:20:45,452 --> 00:20:49,206
You know, not all of our fears come true.

435
00:20:49,790 --> 00:20:52,626
That's why we must not give in to fear.

436
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:55,545
You did say

437
00:20:55,629 --> 00:20:58,131
she left for work.

438
00:20:58,215 --> 00:21:01,301
You also said she takes care of you.

439
00:21:01,385 --> 00:21:04,179
That's why I'm sure

440
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:06,139
that she loves you.

441
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:08,016
Really?

442
00:21:11,436 --> 00:21:14,731
All of us at Angels of Grace
are here for you.

443
00:21:16,733 --> 00:21:23,740
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

444
00:21:30,038 --> 00:21:30,956
[STAFF] Yes, ma'am?

445
00:21:31,039 --> 00:21:32,582
I'm here for Camille.

446
00:21:32,666 --> 00:21:35,460
- Please tell her it's Billy.
- Uh, Billy…

447
00:21:36,253 --> 00:21:37,963
Um, you don't have an appointment.

448
00:21:38,046 --> 00:21:39,548
Just tell her it's Billy.

449
00:21:39,631 --> 00:21:41,008
- Uh--
- I'm sure she knows me.

450
00:21:41,091 --> 00:21:42,968
- Okay, I'll double--
- Call her now.

451
00:21:43,051 --> 00:21:44,303
All right.

452
00:21:46,263 --> 00:21:48,682
[LINE RINGS]

453
00:21:48,765 --> 00:21:54,062
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

454
00:21:54,146 --> 00:21:58,483
[ABI] Thank you, Ms. Camille,
for liking my concept.

455
00:21:59,276 --> 00:22:06,283
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

456
00:22:20,339 --> 00:22:22,591
- [RAIN] <i>You're not jealous anymore.</i>
<i>- We're done.</i>

457
00:22:22,674 --> 00:22:26,595
<i>I would do anything for my mother.</i>
<i>That's why I played with fire.</i>

458
00:22:26,678 --> 00:22:28,889
<i>Billy went through a lot because of her.</i>

459
00:22:28,972 --> 00:22:29,848
<i>She'll get through it.</i>

460
00:22:29,931 --> 00:22:33,060
- [ROBBIE] <i>'Cause you're there for her.</i>
- [JORDAN] <i>She's always there for me too.</i>

461
00:22:33,143 --> 00:22:35,145
[ROBBIE] <i>Ride or die, right?</i>

462
00:22:35,228 --> 00:22:37,773
<i>Billy! What are you doing here?</i>

463
00:22:37,856 --> 00:22:40,358
<i>How did you get your hands</i>
<i>on our LoveFeast concept?</i>

464
00:22:40,442 --> 00:22:41,860
<i>Your concept?</i>

465
00:22:42,527 --> 00:22:44,404
<i>Don't take what's mine!</i>

466
00:22:44,488 --> 00:22:45,530
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GRUNTS]

467
00:22:47,199 --> 00:22:49,117
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [BOTH GRUNT]
